{"Fire-and-forget style in handleCancelBooking.ts - deleteScheduledEmailReminder and deleteScheduledSMSReminder calls are not awaited, causing potential race conditions and inconsistent state": 0.8325388431549072, "deleteScheduledEmailReminder with immediateDelete flag cancels via SendGrid API but does not delete the WorkflowReminder DB row, leading to DB growth, stale references, and inconsistent cancellation semantics": 0.9785255789756775, "Cancellation logic spread across multiple modules (handleNewBooking.ts, handleCancelBooking.ts, TRPC workflows router, scheduleEmailReminders.ts) increases coupling and risk of inconsistent behavior if one path is updated without aligning others": 0.20820064842700958, "New cancelled field on WorkflowReminder is nullable (Boolean?) and migration adds column without default, meaning some reminders may never be picked up by cron if cancelled is null": 0.32822632789611816, "Race condition between cron-final cancellation and immediate cancel paths - concurrent triggers could cause non-deterministic cancellation outcomes without a centralized cancellation manager": 0.44881671667099, "Missing CHANGELOG entry and documentation for the cancellation-flow changes, cron-based final cancellations, and new cancelled field semantics": 0.008307229727506638, "Cron job cancellation logic logs errors but does not escalate them; need to verify API cancellation is robust and idempotent, and that reminders with null referenceId are handled gracefully": 0.2617809772491455, "High churn in handleNewBooking.ts with cancellation logic for rescheduled bookings raises risk of type mismatches, missed edge cases, and race conditions with CRON-based reminder cancellations": 0.09346289187669754, "scheduleEmailReminders.ts may call SendGrid API with null batch_id when referenceId is null, likely resulting in API error - should guard against missing referenceId": 0.9514465928077698, "deleteScheduledEmailReminder signature and logic changed with new immediateDelete flag, potentially causing mismatches between local state and external scheduled sends": 0.7434754371643066, "Broad coupling across high-impact files (Prisma schema, TRPC routers, booking flows, cron endpoints) increases migration risk if semantics are not consistently applied": 0.03997274488210678, "Potential signature drift - residual call-sites may still use old deleteScheduledEmailReminder signature or missing fields in new signature": 0.3141123950481415, "No tests validating new cancelled flag semantics, cron final cancellation, or immediate cancellation paths": 0.24884645640850067, "Missing test guidance and documentation explaining how to test the cancellation flow, cron-based cancellation, and new cancelled field": 0.007079632021486759, "Cancelled reminders flow not covered in cron tests - should mock SendGrid client and verify batch cancel requests and DB deletion": 0.0684003010392189, "deleteScheduledSMSReminder deletes DB row even if external Twilio cancellation fails, leading to loss of traceability and potential inconsistencies": 0.6822221875190735, "Inconsistent usage of immediateDelete flag across call-sites implies inconsistent expectations about cancellation timing": 0.5848149657249451, "UI changes in WorkflowStepContainer for phone verification not reflected in test guidance and docs": 0.0012673601740971208, "Missing E2E test coverage for cron-backed cancellation of scheduled emails": 0.02275865525007248, "New cancelled field on WorkflowReminder not covered by unit/integration tests validating its lifecycle": 0.6182060837745667}